> and/or ran away, I now realize.

Running away works for very short periods of
time but becomes quite problematic for convicts
before long at all, due to the hunger problem.
I've concluded that it is *necessary* for convicts
to do at least some fighting while injured, unless
you get exceptionally lucky finding an unusually
large amount of food on the floor very early.

> 2. Pretty good start; two food rations and a wand
