> I'd had enough daggers already and that skill at basic.

The great thing about daggers is that if you pet-test and
#name one of them, you can do a much faster curse test
on subsequent ones by picking them up and seeing if
they stack.  In my convict games thus far I've managed
by picking up one at a time in this manner to get stacks
of up to four orcish daggers known not to be cursed,
which is very helpful.

> 3. Starved pretty soon; just didn't find enough food.

I've had that, oh, yes.  In my first few times playing as
a convict, I tried to play it like Tourist -- retreating any
time I was injured.  This tactic is no good for a convict,
because you invariably starve.  However, convicts
have enough more strength than Tourists that they
*can*, with sufficient care and a spot of luck, kill (weak)
monsters even when quite low on hitpoints.

> Tried praying when I was as good as dead,
> didn't help me either.  Of course.  ;-)

Right, that's a well documented feature of the role.

I've had one game so far when I made it to the point
where I could safely pray (/ enlightenment FTW).
That's how I found out that even successful prayer
that pleases your diety does not always remove a
ball and chain.

> 4. Found enough food on dlvl 1.  Pet got killed very soon.

I've lost my rat several times.  At least once it got killed.
Another time we got separated by a trap door, and yet
another time I had to flee and could not go back for my
pet on pain of death.

Thing is, I don't think losing your pet is really worse for a
Convict than for, say, a Tourist.  Well, okay, there's the
problem that you won't be able to easily replace it with
another pet of the same kind (because rats aren't as easy
to tame as dogs and cats and horses), but if you aren't
attached (by emotion or role playing) to having the "right"
pet type for your role, that isn't really a big deal:  a Convict
can throw tripe at the next dog they see just as easily as
any other role.

Of course, the "ascend with your original pet" challenge
would be especially interesting for a Convict, but that's
really an advanced activity, like conducts and whatnot.

> then went down to dlvl 2 =96 half of my 14 HP gone by
