I like them in the sense that they make this role distinctive
and add meaningful variety and challenge to the role system,
which is good.  I don't know that Convict will soon be my
favorite role to play (frankly, I'm not good enough to really
need quite that much challenge yet), but I like the concept.

> Eating zombies and suchlike without regret is a major
> advantage for the convict, especially regarding his
> shortcomings.

It does help mitigate the hunger problem a little and
would probably come in handy later in the game if
you manage to make it that far.

> I also like eating the lichens the rat sometimes scatters
> around in dungeon without having to consider their age.

Umm, any role can eat lichens of any age.  (Lichens
are special in this regard.  They do not spoil, ever.
You can safely eat them after ten thousand turns.)
However, substitute virtually any other monster type
(that the rat is capable of killing) in place of "lichens",
and your observation becomes valid.  You can wander
up to a pet kill having no idea how long it's been on
the floor and go ahead and eat it.  This is an important
survival tactic for Convicts, since they start hungry
with no food and a positive prayer timeout.

